docs/papers122_126_sequence/scouting/algebraic/SCOUT.md:15:This pass defined 20 literal finite dynamical systems across matrix algebras, subspace and ideal lattices, finite groups, and truncated/path algebras. Twelve were implemented in an exact deterministic standard-library pilot. The run made **3,673,684 assertions** and passed. Strict subtraction leaves three candidates with an early theorem-shaped signal (C1, C3, C6), two reserves whose first invariant is real but whose temporal theorem is not yet closed (C8, C12), and fifteen killed or parked controls.
docs/papers122_126_sequence/scouting/algebraic/SCOUT.md:55:| C3 | On (\operatorname{Sub}(\mathbb F_q^d)^2), (T(U,V)=(V,U+N(V))). | Closed semiring-Fibonacci iterates, eventual periods only 1 or 2, and pilot-sharp maximum transient (d). | **PROMOTE TO PROOF DOSSIER.** Static nilpotent-subspace literature is substantial, but the exact recurrence was not found. |
docs/papers122_126_sequence/scouting/algebraic/SCOUT.md:62:| C10 | On (H_p^2), for the finite Heisenberg group (H_p), (T(x,y)=(y,xy)). | Exact pilot cycle censuses: (p=2:{1:1,3:9,6:6}), (p=3:{1:1,8:91}), (p=5:{1:1,4:31,20:775}), (p=7:{1:1,16:7353}). | **KILL:** classical Nielsen transformation plus severe internal collision with the earlier Heisenberg word/area lane. |
docs/papers122_126_sequence/scouting/algebraic/SCOUT.md:63:| C11 | Hurwitz map on (G^2), tested on (H_p^2): (T(x,y)=(y,y^{-1}xy)). | (xy) is invariant, (T^2) is simultaneous conjugation by (xy), and cycles in (H_p^2) divide (2p). | **KILL:** this is the standard two-strand Hurwitz action. |
docs/papers122_126_sequence/scouting/algebraic/SCOUT.md:64:| C12 | On (M_2(\mathbb F_q)^2), (T(A,B)=(AB,BA)). | Both component ranks decrease; exhaustive maxima are depth/cycle (3/2) for (q=2) and (5/4) for (q=3). | **RESERVE.** Genuine noncommutative coupling, but no general depth/cycle theorem and high AB/BA-owner density. |
docs/papers122_126_sequence/scouting/algebraic/SCOUT.md:71:| C19 | On (M_2(\mathbb F_q)^2), (T(A,B)=(AB-BA,AB+BA)). | The two outputs collapse together in characteristic two; odd characteristic permits recovery of (AB,BA). | **PARK:** a sharp characteristic threshold exists, but it is presently only a coordinate change of product data, not a closed dynamical theorem. |
