papers/67-multiplicative-plaquette-matroid-complexity/stage4/REVISED_DRAFT.md:24: \qquad \epsilon_n(x)=x_n,\qquad n\in F.\] Thus \(A\subseteq F\) is independent when the functionals \(\{\epsilon_n:n\in A\}\) are linearly independent. This is the standard linear-dependence meaning of matroid terminology \[@Whitney1935\]. For normalized Haar measure \(\mu\) on \(X_{a,b}\) and the random vector \(Z_F=(x_n)_{n\in F}\), write \[\TC_\mu(Z_F)=\sum_{n\in F}\Ent_\mu(x_n)-\Ent_\mu(Z_F)\] for its total correlation.
